{"name":"Komodo Dragon","hex":"#b38052","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"komodo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Komodo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/komodo"},{"term":"dragon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical reptilian or serpentine creature.","In European mythologies, a gigantic beast, typically reptilian with leathery bat-like wings, lion-like claws, scaly skin and a lizard-like body, often a monster with fiery breath."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of drag queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Komodo dragon","blocks":[{"text":"The Komodo dragon, also known as the Komodo monitor, is a large reptile of the monitor lizard family Varanidae that is endemic to the Indonesian islands of Komodo, Rinca, Flores, Gili Dasami, and Gili Motang. The largest extant population lives within the Komodo National Park in Eastern Indonesia. It is the largest extant species of lizard, with the males growing to a maximum length of 3 m (10 ft) and weighing up to 150 kg (330 lb)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/202306_Varanus_komodoensis.jpg/330px-202306_Varanus_komodoensis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komodo_dragon","wikidata":"Q4504"},{"title":"Komodo (island)","blocks":[{"text":"Komodo is one of the 17,508 islands that comprise the Republic of Indonesia. It is particularly notable as the habitat of the Komodo dragon, the largest lizard on Earth, which is named after the island. Komodo Island has a surface area of 291 square kilometres, and had a human population of about 1,800 in 2020."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Komodo_Island_north_aerial.jpg/330px-Komodo_Island_north_aerial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komodo_(island)","wikidata":"Q107640"},{"title":"Komodo (chess)","blocks":[{"text":"Komodo and Dragon by Komodo Chess are UCI chess engines developed by Komodo Chess, which is a part of Chess.com. The engines were originally authored by Don Dailey and GM Larry Kaufman. Dragon is a commercial chess engine, but Komodo is free for non-commercial use. Dragon is consistently ranked near the top of most major chess engine rating lists, along with Stockfish and Leela Chess Zero."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Chess_Programming.svg/330px-Chess_Programming.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Komodo_(chess)","wikidata":"Q6428455"},{"title":"Dragon","blocks":[{"text":"A dragon is a mythical creature found in the folklore of cultures throughout the world. It is roughly serpentine in form, and often possesses features drawn from different animals, such as wings and claws. In nearly all cultures, it is conceived of as a powerful and awe-inspiring creature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png/330px-St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon","wikidata":"Q7559"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Komodo_dragon_distribution.gif/500px-Komodo_dragon_distribution.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Komodo_dragon_distribution.gif/500px-Komodo_dragon_distribution.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten